# C03 route action transport — DO NOT APPLY

Issue: https://github.com/liboyang42-cpu/chengyin-remote-ops/issues/5
Repo: github.com/liboyang42-cpu/chengyin-ios
Base: cursor/c03-route-page-caller-e504 @ c1d77d7c0f591677dada89e80ca7765fa652cb84
Branch: cursor/c03-route-action-transport-e504

DO NOT APPLY this hunk. Do not edit App/AppSession.swift, App/AppCompositionRoot.swift, or Questify.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj from this branch.

The installed read is GET /api/play/route-action. It uses the existing current member id and TopicRouteSessionMapper.selectActionByAction. It does not insert a route action.

`App/PlayRouteMapView.swift` sends that GET on the host already present on the held https APIConfiguration. The query carries sessionId, memberId, and actionId. A row is shown only when the response session id, member id, and action id equal the request. A mismatch shows nothing.

A missing configuration, a non-https URL, a blank token, or account id 0 closes only this read and does not invent a domain. The previously held serviceResult is not a network read. This branch does not return it.

## Why the session must pass configuration, transport, token, and member id

`compositionTransport` is private (`App/AppSession.swift` around line 188). `token` is private (around line 3255). `PlayExperienceView` does not hold either of them. `SessionPlayRuntimeView` only has the session. Passing the held `regionalConfiguration?.apiConfiguration`, `compositionTransport`, the raw token, and `account.id` into `PlayRouteMapView.actionRead` can be done only from inside AppSession.

This branch does not add that method. `PlayRouteMapView` is already in the app target. No new PBX file reference is required for the send. Do not edit pbxproj.

## Not applied

```
App/AppSession.swift
App/AppCompositionRoot.swift
Questify.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj
App/MessagingHomeView.swift
App/ProfileOrdersView.swift
MerchantDeskSkuPage.swift
```

Unapplied method, beside `playExperience(for:)` (around line 363). Do not apply.

```swift
func routeActionPageRead(sessionID: Int64, actionID: String) -> RouteActionPageReadRequest? {
    guard let configuration = regionalConfiguration?.apiConfiguration,
          let account, account.id != 0, let token, AuthRequestBuilder.isValidToken(token) else { return nil }
    return RouteActionPageReadRequest(
        sessionID: sessionID,
        memberID: Int64(account.id),
        actionID: actionID,
        apiBaseURL: configuration.baseURL,
        transport: compositionTransport,
        token: token,
        accountID: account.id)
}
```

`serviceResult` is not an argument. A caller-held row is not a network read. The page sends GET /api/play/route-action on `configuration.baseURL` and does not invent a domain. Account id 0 and a blank token return nil and close only this read.

Unapplied call, not inserted into `PlayExperienceView` or `SessionPlayRuntimeView`:

```swift
PlayRouteMapView(
    model: model,
    nodeDestination: { AnyView(nodeDestination($0)) },
    actionRead: session.routeActionPageRead(sessionID: sessionID, actionID: actionID))
```

`session.routeActionPageRead` does not exist. Do not add it on this branch. Until that attach exists, `actionRead` stays nil: no row and no send. Not a second writer. `AppCompositionRoot` is not edited, so this paste does not open another composition route.

XCTest / App / CI = NOT_RUN. swiftc was not required to land this file. Not 100%.
